<https://hexplain.io/ns/audio#AudioStream> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An ordered audio sample stream whose sampling, channel and encoding properties are described separately."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/audio#AudioStream> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for audio resources, their streams and source metadata. Sampling, encoding and timing aspects carry shared properties. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/audio#MetadataTag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A metadata-bearing component carrying descriptive information about an audio work or recording."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/audio#MetadataTag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for audio resources, their streams and source metadata. Sampling, encoding and timing aspects carry shared properties. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/audio#StreamShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for aenc:bitrate, aenc:codec, asamp:bitDepth, asamp:componentCount, asig:sampleRate, atime:duration. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
